%% The development organisation — who reports to whom, who talks, who gates
flowchart TB
  OP(["OPERATOR<br/>rules design forks · checkrides · walks into any room"])
  FD["FRONT DESK (persistent, view-only)<br/>one queue of events from every room<br/>points the operator AT the room that needs them"]
  ORCH["ORCHESTRATOR (persistent)<br/>cursor · grounding probe → charters · COLLECTS residue<br/>checkpoint watcher → initiates design sessions<br/>micro-task tier · may charter AD-HOC rooms"]
  ARCH["ARCHITECT (persistent — the future)<br/>corpus: angles · current→target map · design D# log<br/>works per-CHECKPOINT on the residue collection<br/>conformance reports · never tactical, never blocks"]
  R1["ITEM ROOM ×N (ephemeral — the present)<br/>OWNS its worktree: create → work → FF-CAS merge → retire<br/>SDD inside (role-split: implementer · reviewer · follow-up)<br/>resolves discrepancies locally · plants MARKERS · files residue"]

  ORCH -->|reports to| OP
  ARCH -->|reports to| OP
  FD -->|reports to| ORCH
  R1 -->|reports to| ORCH

  ORCH <-.->|peers · info| ARCH
  ADHOC["AD-HOC ROOM (orchestrator-chartered)<br/>probe · spike · sweep — foreign skill mixes<br/>kept out of the architect room"]
  ADHOC -->|reports to| ORCH
  R1 <-.->|peers · info: corpus questions| ARCH
  R1 -.->|events| FD
  ARCH -.->|events: agenda ripe| FD
  ORCH -.->|queue| FD

  G2{{"gate · approval<br/>OPERATOR rules design sessions —<br/>angle/map changes bind only when ruled"}}
  ARCH --- G2 --- OP
  G3{{"gate · veto<br/>GROUNDING PROBE gates chartering —<br/>no item room without a measured census"}}
  ORCH --- G3 --- R1
  G4{{"gate · script<br/>FF-CAS publish recipe (mechanical) —<br/>merge always possible, never architect-blocked"}}
  R1 --- G4
  G5{{"gate · veto<br/>room CLOSE requires worktree merged & retired<br/>(orchestrator verifies; the 30-dead-worktrees fix)"}}
  ORCH --- G5 --- R1
